  "name": "CakeML",
  "description": "CakeML is a verified implementation of a significant subset of Standard ML, developed within the HOL4 theorem prover. It features a bootstrapped, end-to-end verified compiler that targets multiple architectures including x86-64, ARM, and RISC-V. The project provides a formally verified ecosystem encompassing a standard basis library, a verified HOL theorem prover (Candle), and characteristic formulae for program verification.",
